# Agent Instructions

Keep these three repository skills always active unless the user explicitly disables them (`stop caveman`, `stop ponytail`, `stop humanizer`, or `normal mode`):

1. **`caveman`** (`.agents/skills/caveman/SKILL.md`): Terse, answer-first communication for all chat responses.
2. **`ponytail`** (`.agents/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md`): Lazy senior dev mode (`full` default) for all coding tasks — solve the complete task with the smallest working diff, verify callers and tests, and close replies with skipped items or risks in 1–2 lines.
3. **`humanizer`** (`.agents/skills/humanizer/SKILL.md`): Remove AI writing patterns from all written prose, documentation, README updates, release notes, and PR descriptions.

- Keep code, comments, commit messages, and documentation in clean, natural prose (no caveman voice in persisted files).
- Preserve exact file paths, commands, symbols, error lines, and security warnings.
